tion? @state)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-352-      (swap! state assoc :resolution? true)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:353:      (emit! state attachment :ws/transport-error))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-354-    (terminal! state attachment (if (= ended-close-code code) :ws/ended :ws/closed))))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-355-\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-356-\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-357-(defn adapter\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-358-  \"The only callback-shaped value, for a host socket adapter while wiring its\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:359:   private listener.  It is not a DaoStream API and never reaches consumers.\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-360-   `:message!` receives text frames and `:binary!` binary frames — the two\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-361-   typed facts a host reports without inspecting content — and `:ws/codec`\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-362-   is the connection's profile, so a host `:connect!` seam can negotiate the\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-363-   selected subprotocol without any second channel.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-364-  [handle]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-365-  {:opened! #(opened! handle)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-366-   :disclaimed! #(disclaimed! handle)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-367-   :message! #(receive! handle %)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-368-   :binary! #(receive-binary! handle %)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-369-   :closed! #(closed! handle %1 %2)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-370-   :ws/codec (.-codec ^WsHandle handle)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-371-   :error! #(emit-reason! (.-state ^WsHandle handle) (.-attachment ^WsHandle handle)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-372-                          :ws/error :ws/socket-error)})\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-373-\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-374-\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:375:(defn make-attacher\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-376-  \"Construct the host-composed unary `attach!` entry point.\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-377-\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-378-   `:connect!` receives the descriptor and the private adapter map, starts\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-379-   connection establishment, and synchronously returns a raw-socket adapter\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-380-   containing `:send!` and `:close!`.  It must not wait for the peer.\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-381-\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-382-   `:codec` selects the wire profile explicitly (default: Transit).  The\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-383-   offer is exactly the selected subprotocol, so a peer that does not speak\n--\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-395-              [handle state] (new-handle descriptor id target :connecting nil codec)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-396-          (try\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-397-            (let [socket (connect! descriptor (adapter handle))]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-398-              (if (and (map? socket) (fn? (:send! socket)) (fn? (:close! socket)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-399-                (do (swap! state assoc :socket socket)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-400-                    {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-401-                     :dao.stream/handle handle\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-402-                     :dao.stream/attachment id})\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:403:                (outcome :dao.stream/transport-error)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-404-            (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:405:              (outcome :dao.stream/transport-error))))))))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-406-\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-407-\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-408-;; Server acceptance is intentionally an endpoint composition object, not a\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-409-;; global transport directory.  Its slots are supplied and owned by the host.\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-410-(defn make-endpoint\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-411-  [{:keys [served control control-admission slots codecs] :as config}]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-412-  (let [control-target (checked-target control control-admission)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-413-        codecs (or codecs [transit/profile])]\n--\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-513-           (do (invoke-close! socket 1013 \"dao.stream/acceptance-full\")\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-514-               {:ws/status :ws/full})\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-515-           (let [[index slot] @chosen\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-516-                 id (attachment-id)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-517-                 [handle hstate] (new-handle descriptor id (endpoint-target endpoint) :pending socket codec)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-518-                 offer {:ws/attachment id :ws/event :ws/accepted\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-519-                        :ws/handle {:dao.stream/handle handle\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-520-                                    :dao.stream/surface #{:writer :closable}}}\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc:521:                 result (stream/append! (:dao.stream/handle (:offer slot)) offer)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-522-             (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-523-               (do (swap! state (fn [s]\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-524-                                  (-> s\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-525-                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :status] :pending)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-526-                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :attachment] id)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-527-                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :handle] handle)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-528-                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :handle-state] hstate)\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc-529-                                      (assoc-in [:slots index :codec] codec)\n--\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:1:# DaoStream Design\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-2-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:3:Status: agreed design target. This document is the DaoStream contract. It does\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-4-not redesign Yin.VM. Yin.VM is a downstream consumer and will be addressed only\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-5-after this contract is implemented and tested.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-6-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-7-## Purpose\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-8-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-9-This contract derives from the foundational axioms and non-negotiable\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-10-invariants of [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md). Two axioms bear on it\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-11-directly, named here once so the sections below can cite rather than restate\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-12-them:\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-13-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-14-1. **Everything is a Stream** — all IO and data flow through append-only\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-15-   streams.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-16-2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics** — data is syntax; semantics emerge\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-17-   only through interpretation. One truth, many perspectives.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-18-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:19:DaoStream is the passive substrate for IO in datom.world — passive because\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-20-interpretation and execution must not collapse into one layer. Axiom 1 is\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-21-what makes this the layer every host boundary crosses. A stream carries\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-22-values and decides nothing about them:\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-23-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-24-- **What the values mean** is not its business — Axiom 2. An element\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-25-  judged, filtered, or typed at this layer destroys the perspectives nobody\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-26-  has taken yet.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-27-- **Which interpreter observes them** is not recorded — a registry of who\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-28-  is listening would be hidden global state.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-29-- **When an interpreter runs** is not its decision — \"do not introduce\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-30-  callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream\", seen from the stream's\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:31:  side: DaoStream invokes nothing, so control is never inverted and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-32-  causality stays explicit (see The IO Model).\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-33-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-34-The Invariants below are these denials in operational form.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-35-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-36-The design separates five concepts:\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-37-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-38-1. A **creation specification** is data for creating a new logical stream.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-39-2. A **handle** is a host-local operational stream value — the\n--\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-54-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-55-| Operation    | Consumes               | Yields             |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-56-|--------------|------------------------|--------------------|\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-57-| `create!`    | creation specification | handle outcome     |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-58-| `attach!`    | portable descriptor    | handle outcome     |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-59-| `descriptor` | handle                 | descriptor outcome |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-60-| `cursor`     | handle, anchor         | cursor outcome     |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-61-| `next`       | handle, cursor         | read outcome       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:62:| `append!`    | handle, value          | write outcome      |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-63-| `close!`     | handle                 | close outcome      |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-64-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-65-A handle implements the subset of the **handle surface** its transport\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-66-declares (see Surfaces). `create!` and `attach!` are not part of it: they\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-67-consume no handle and produce one.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-68-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-69-## Invariants\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-70-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:71:- Stream elements are data. DaoStream assigns them no intrinsic meaning.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-72-- Reading is non-destructive. A reader advances its own cursor, not the stream.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-73-- Multiple cursors may observe the same retained value independently.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-74-- Interpreters own cursors and decide when to call `next`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:75:- A runtime may drive an interpreter, but DaoStream does not require a runtime.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-76-- Closing a stream changes future availability but does not itself erase\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-77-  retained history.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-78-- Retention may be bounded. A cursor over evicted history receives a gap\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-79-  outcome as data; the reader decides what missing data means.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-80-- All expected operational outcomes are data, not exceptions or callbacks.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-81-- No operation waits. Every operation returns what is true at the moment it is\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-82-  called; an answer not yet knowable arrives later as data.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:83:- No hidden global state. DaoStream keeps no registry of streams, handles, or\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-84-  observers, and no operation consults ambient state.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-85-- A logical stream has an identity that is plain data, the same through every\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-86-  handle on it, stable across attachment lifecycles and across serialization.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-87-  Projecting that identity never fails.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-88-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-89-Every clause below must be consistent with these invariants, and most derive\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-90-from one directly. Where a clause is instead an interoperability decision — the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-91-descriptor's properties, the result keyword namespace, the anchor set — it is\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-92-stated as a decision rather than dressed as a deduction. A proposed addition\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-93-that contradicts an invariant does not belong in this contract; one that merely\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-94-cannot be deduced from them must say which decision it is and why.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-95-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-96-## Result Convention\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-97-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:98:Every DaoStream operation returns data.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-99-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-100-- Each operation's set of outcomes is **exhaustive**: a transport may produce\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-101-  fewer of them, never any outside the set. Which subset it produces is part of\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-102-  its declared nature (see Surfaces). An outcome is a map whose\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-103-  `:dao.stream/outcome` key names the outcome with a qualified keyword. Every\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-104-  operation returns such a map — including projections like `descriptor` and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-105-  `cursor`, whose success map carries the projected value.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-106-- `:dao.stream/outcome` is present in every result map and is never repeated\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-107-  in the per-outcome tables below; the keys those tables name are required in\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-108-  addition to it.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-109-- Result maps are **open**: the contract fixes which keys are required per\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-110-  outcome, and a consumer must ignore keys it does not understand. This is\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-111-  what allows future extensions (for example readiness notification) to be\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-112-  added without breaking existing consumers.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-113-- Exceptions are reserved for defects in the host's own assembly of\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:114:  DaoStream, detected before any operation runs. Everything observable at an\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:115:  operation returns data: closed, full, blocked, end, gap, not found,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-116-  malformed input, and transport defects are all outcomes, never exceptions\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-117-  and never callbacks.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-118-- All qualified keywords in results live under `:dao.stream/…`.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-119-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-120-## The IO Model\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-121-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:122:Three models are available for expressing IO. DaoStream is deliberately the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-123-third.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-124-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-125-**Blocking (synchronous) IO.** The operation parks until it has an answer,\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-126-then returns it. Control flow stays sequential and the call site reads as\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-127-ordinary code, which is the whole of its appeal. The cost is that something\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-128-must wait — a thread per pending operation, held for its duration — and it\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-129-requires a host that can park at all.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-130-\n--\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-136-without blocking, a promise cannot be absorbed inside a function, because\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-137-awaiting returns to the caller at the first suspension point and makes the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-138-caller's own result a promise in turn. Whatever is reached from a callback\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-139-is reached from a callback.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-140-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-141-**Non-blocking polling.** The operation returns immediately with whatever is\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-142-true now, including the answer \"nothing yet, ask again.\" Nothing parks and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-143-nothing is inverted: the caller keeps control and decides when to ask again.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:144:This is POSIX `O_NONBLOCK` without `select`, and it is DaoStream's model.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-145-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-146-`next` is total and non-blocking (see Reading): every state of the stream\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:147:has a defined data answer, and `:dao.stream/blocked` is `EAGAIN` — this\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:148:position holds nothing yet. `append!`'s `:dao.stream/full` is the same\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-149-answer for writes. No operation in this contract parks, and none takes a\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-150-callback; the Result Convention's \"never exceptions and never callbacks\" is\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-151-this model stated as a rule about results.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-152-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-153-The rule generalizes past `next`: **no operation waits.** An operation that\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-154-cannot yet know its answer returns the outcome true at the moment it is\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-155-called, and the eventual answer arrives the way every other fact does — as\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-156-data, observed later, through an ordinary operation or on a stream. A\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:157:DaoStream operation is never a request for something to happen and be\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-158-reported back. It is a question about now.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-159-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-160-### Why this model and not the other two\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-161-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-162-The hosts do not offer the same choices. The JVM has both blocking and\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-163-asynchronous IO. JavaScript and Dart have only the asynchronous kind: there\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-164-is no blocking read to call and no way to wait for one, because the single\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-165-event loop that would deliver the answer is the one a waiting call would be\n--\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-174-differing by host.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-175-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-176-### What it 