eam.md-535-It is total and non-blocking: every state of the stream has a defined data\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-536-answer.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-537-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-538-| Outcome                       | Meaning                                                                       | Required keys                                                                           |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-539-|-------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-540-| `:dao.stream/ok`              | A value was observed.                                                         | `:dao.stream/value`, `:dao.stream/cursor` (successor)                                   |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:541:| `:dao.stream/blocked`         | Nothing at this position yet; retry later.                                    | —                                                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-542-| `:dao.stream/end`             | What this handle is on is closed and this position is past the retained tail. | —                                                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-543-| `:dao.stream/gap`             | This position was evicted.                                                    | `:dao.stream/cursor` (earliest retained position, or the tail when nothing is retained) |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-544-| `:dao.stream/cursor-mismatch` | The cursor was minted by a different logical stream.                          | —                                                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-545-| `:dao.stream/invalid-cursor`  | The value is not a cursor.                                                    | —                                                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:546:| `:dao.stream/transport-error` | The transport failed to perform the read; nothing was observed.               | —                                                                                       |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-547-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-548-Reading never mutates the stream. Two readers with cursors at the same\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-549-position observe the same retained value; neither can starve or affect the\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-550-other. There is no destructive read anywhere in the contract — no drain, no\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-551-take. An operation that removes an element as it reads would make one\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-552-reader's progress every other reader's data loss.\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-553-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-554-## Writing\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-555-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md:556:`append!` takes a handle and a value and returns an outcome:\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-557-\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-558-| Outcome                       | Meaning                                                                                                                                              | Required keys |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-559-|-------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------|\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-560-| `:dao.stream/ok`              | The value is accepted at the next position in the sequence this handle's writer surface is on. Implies neither local readability nor remote delivery. | —             |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md-561-| `:dao.stream/full`            | The transport does not accept the value; nothing was appended. Whether this is transient or permanent is the transport's declared nature (see Retention and Gaps). | —             |\ndocs/design/dao.stream.md